<title>FRANCE: French police make major drugs haul.</title>
<headline>French police make major drugs haul.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>French police seized three tonnes of Morocco cannabis on Friday and arrested four men, Interior Minister Jean-Louis Debre announced.</p>
<p>Debre told a news conference the drugs, valued at 45 million francs ($7.7 million), were tracked fromTangiers to France in a joint operation with Moroccan police and seized in the Alpine Savoie region. Those detained were French and Moroccan.</p>
</text>
